# Tailwind conventions

## Utility ordering

Order classes consistently so diffs stay readable:
layout (display, position) → box model (w/h, margin, padding) → typography →
color/background → border → effects (shadow, opacity) → transitions →
states (`hover:` `focus:`) → responsive (`md:` `lg:`).

## Responsive

- Mobile-first. Write base styles, then layer `sm:` `md:` `lg:`. Never
  desktop-first with overrides.
- Use the project's configured breakpoints. Don't invent arbitrary
  `[width:1037px]` values without a clear reason.

## Component extraction

- If the same class string repeats 3+ times, extract a component — don't
  `@apply` it into a CSS file.
- Don't create a wrapper component for a single use. Inline is fine until it
  actually repeats.

## Design tokens

- Use theme tokens (colors, spacing, fonts) from `tailwind.config`. Never
  hardcode hex values or one-off pixel values that duplicate an existing token.
- Need a new recurring value? Add it to the theme first, then use the token.

## Don't

- No inline `style=` when a utility exists.
- No `!important` / `!` prefix unless overriding third-party CSS — and comment
  why when you do.
